# Sahayak AI - Mock Demo Walkthrough

The mock demo environment has been successfully set up. It uses a custom `MOCK_MODE` to bypass AWS dependencies (DynamoDB, Bedrock, Comprehend) and instead relies on local seed data and hardcoded responses. This enables a fully functional, local "juggad" demo for video recording purposes while preserving the system's modular architecture!

## Changes Made

1. **[rule_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/eligibility-engine/src/rules/rule_engine.py) (EligibilityRuleEngine)**: Intercepts [_get_rules()](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/eligibility-engine/src/rules/rule_engine.py#178-207) when `MOCK_MODE=1` is present. It dynamically loads the `ELIGIBILITY_RULES` from [scripts/seed_schemes.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/scripts/seed_schemes.py) rather than querying the DynamoDB table.
2. **[bedrock_client.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/bedrock/bedrock_client.py) (BedrockOrchestrator)**: Intercepts [generate_response()](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/bedrock/bedrock_client.py#22-104). Bypasses `boto3` execution and simulates a 1-second network call latency. If the query mentions PM Kisan, it returns a hardcoded summary of the scheme along with mocked `action_items`.
3. **[language_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/voice-service/src/processors/language_detector.py) (LanguageDetector)**: Bypasses the Amazon Comprehend fallback and defaults to [hi](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/eligibility-engine/src/rules/rule_engine.py#213-221) (Hindi) if the regex heuristic cannot confidently detect the language.
4. **[mock_demo.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/mock_demo.py)**: A brand new **Streamlit** frontend script that ties the entire backend together. It configures the Python Path to import from the `services/` directory and instantiates all the major AI components ([LanguageDetector](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/voice-service/src/processors/language_detector.py#14-49), [IntentClassifier](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/orchestration/intent_classifier.py#64-105), [BedrockOrchestrator](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/bedrock/bedrock_client.py#17-176), [EligibilityRuleEngine](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/eligibility-engine/src/rules/rule_engine.py#49-240), [DataMasker](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/user-profile-service/src/privacy/data_masker.py#8-59)).

## How to use the Demo

The Streamlit UI has automatically been started on your local terminal! 

You can interact with it by doing the following:

- **Data Privacy Demonstration**: Look at the sidebar on the left. You will see a mock user profile. Just below it, the [DataMasker](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/user-profile-service/src/privacy/data_masker.py#8-59) output is displayed, showing how the name, phone number, and Aadhaar are masked before logging (DPDP compliance).
- **Eligibility Checking**: In the chat box at the bottom, type `"Am I eligible?"` or `"क्या मैं पात्र हूँ?"`. The [IntentClassifier](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/orchestration/intent_classifier.py#64-105) will intercept this as an `eligibility_check`. The [EligibilityRuleEngine](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/eligibility-engine/src/rules/rule_engine.py#49-240) will evaluate the mock user profile from the sidebar against the criteria from [seed_schemes.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/scripts/seed_schemes.py) and print whether the citizen is `ELIGIBLE` or `INELIGIBLE`, and outline exactly which criteria passed/failed.
- **Scheme Information Query**: Type `"Tell me about PM Kisan"`. The LLM Orchestrator will trigger and stream back the hardcoded bedrock response about PM Kisan.

You can modify the user profile in the sidebar (e.g. changing income or acreage) and re-run the eligibility check to show different outcomes in real-time.

> [!TIP]
> If you close the terminal, you can restart the demo at any time by navigating to your repository root and running: `streamlit run mock_demo.py`
>
> **Containerized Version:**
> You can also run this mock demo using Docker! This ensures all dependencies are encapsulated and matches our broader architecture strategy.
> 1. Stop any local Streamlit process.
> 2. Run: `docker-compose up -d`
> 3. Open `http://localhost:8501` in your browser.

## Phase 2: Natural Conversation & Mobile UI Enhancements

To make the demo feel more authentic and closer to the end vision of a voice-first application:

1. **Mobile UI Simulation**: We injected custom HTML/CSS into the Streamlit app to constrain the width, add rounded corners, hide the default Streamlit header, and style the chat bubbles like a modern messaging app (e.g. WhatsApp/iMessage).
2. **"Voice Input" Simulation**: A dropdown was added to simulate voice inputs. This enables you to easily click complex queries like `"Am I eligible for PMJDY?"` to demonstrate language understanding without typing.
3. **Conversational Responses**: The fallback mocked LLM logic in [BedrockOrchestrator](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/services/conversation-orchestrator/src/bedrock/bedrock_client.py#17-176) was updated to handle basic greetings ("Hello", "नमस्ते") in a friendly, conversational manner. It also now supports information retrieval for **PM Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY)** alongside **PM Kisan**.
4. **Enriched Seed Data**: Added mock scheme logic for `PMJDY-2024` into [seed_schemes.py](file:///c:/Users/bhawu/Documents/GitHub/SahayakAI-Dev/scripts/seed_schemes.py), allowing the engine to parse eligibility criteria specifically for that scheme.

You can test these out right now in the running interface!
